🧠 Comprehensive marker check reveals several mismatches with CellTypist's fine labels:

- **Clusters 0 & 1** ("Intermediate macrophages"): High CD14, LYZ, FCN1, S100A8 — classic classical monocyte markers, not tissue macrophages (which shouldn't appear in blood).
- **Cluster 4** ("NK cells"): CD3D is significantly enriched (66.4% vs 29.2% elsewhere) alongside CD8A/CD8B/GZMB/NKG7/GNLY — this is a CD3+ population, i.e., cytotoxic/effector CD8 T cells, not NK cells (contrast with cluster 11, true NK, where CD3D is depleted). The high-resolution model agrees, calling it "T cells."
- **Cluster 12** ("Tcm/Naive helper T cells"): PPBP, PF4, ITGA2B are massively enriched — this is clearly platelets, not T cells.

Other clusters check out (cluster 2 = FCGR3A/MS4A7+ non-classical monocytes; cluster 9 = LILRA4/GZMB+ pDC; cluster 10 = CD1C/FCER1A+ DC2; cluster 11 = CD3D-negative GNLY/NKG7+ NK; cluster 13 = CD79A/MS4A1/CD19+ B cells; cluster 14 = HBB/HBA1+ erythroid; cluster 15 = TPSAB1+ rare mast cells, CD3D-negative). Let me relabel the three problematic clusters.
🔧 relabel_clusters(labels={'0': 'CD14+ Classical monocytes', '1': 'CD14+ Classical monocytes', '4': 'CD8+ Effector T cells', '12': 'Platelets'}, reason=Cluster 0/1: CellTypist called these 'Intermediate macrophages' but markers (CD14 log2FC~2.4-4.6 in 40-64% of cells, LYZ in 72-84%, FCN1 in 55-79%, S100A8 in 60-78%) are canonical classical monocyte markers; tissue macrophages are not expected in PBMC blood samples. Cluster 4: labeled 'NK cells' but CD3D is significantly enriched (66.4% pct-in vs 29.2% elsewhere, log2FC 2.34, padj~0) together with CD8A/CD8B, GZMB, NKG7, GNLY -- a CD3+ cytotoxic/effector CD8 T cell profile, not NK (contrast with true NK cluster 11 where CD3D is depleted: 4.5% vs 35.1% elsewhere). The coarse CellTypist model independently calls cluster 4 'T cells', agreeing with this correction. Cluster 12: labeled 'Tcm/Naive helper T cells' but PPBP (85.1% cells, log2FC 7.7), PF4 (63.6%, log2FC 7.46), and ITGA2B (7.4%, log2FC 6.76) are all massively and specifically enriched -- unambiguous platelet markers, not T cells.)
   → changes, cell_type_counts, checkpoint

