a decrease in DC2 ({{comp.dc2.ctrl}} -> {{comp.dc2.stim}}, padj {{comp.dc2.padj}}) and an
increase in pDC ({{comp.pdc.ctrl}} -> {{comp.pdc.stim}}, padj {{comp.pdc.padj}}), but neither
survived correction and pDC could only be tested with very few cells per sample. With only 8
paired donors, the paired Wilcoxon test cannot reach significance below p=0.0078 even in the
best case, so this analysis is under-powered to detect anything but large, consistent shifts;
a true absence of compositional change over this short (6h) stimulation is also biologically
plausible, since PBMC subset frequencies are not expected to shift substantially without cell
death/proliferation over such a short window.

